  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 73ff519377b990a4c81cd1461a3c1f62, type: 3}
  m_Name: Klara_W40_Teach
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueNode
  speakerName: Klara
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: cf385c5c4168f354ca622b8557a81b73, type: 3}
  dialogueText: 'Ti sumaruno a numero ket ''tallo.''


    Iti Ilokano, ti ''tallo''
    ket kayatna a saoen ti ''three.''


    Kas pagarigan, mabalinmo nga agusar iti
    daytoy no agbilangka iti tallo a banag.


    Denggem a naimbag: tallo.


    Ita,
    padasem nga ibagam ti ''tallo'' iti bukodmo a timek.'
  translatedText: 'The next number is ''tallo.''

    In Ilokano, ''tallo'' means
    ''three.''

    For example, you can use it when counting three objects.

    Now,
    try saying ''tallo'' yourself.'
